      "comment": "ALAA PLENTY (6) gets the nod despite two plain eighths since resuming, with the strength of his past 12 months, his record at around 1100m and the Gary Clarke-Jarrod Todd combination giving him the most compelling profile. He was beaten just under five lengths in a BM64 at Murray Bdge last start and is now third-up at his first run in this state, so there is a clear platform for improvement. STEAMY MIST (8) is the immediate danger after a well-supported win at this track, where she beat Tears Are Flowing by two and a half lengths and now gets weight relief. KING AKEED (4) also arrives off a first-up win, scoring in BM64 grade at this venue, and his 1100m record keeps him right in the mix despite the grade rise. TEXTURE (5) resumes with a perfect three-from-three record at this track and barrier 1, but his last-start Kununurra defeat means he has more to prove fresh.",
